<LegalLayout title="Subprocessors and Retention" description="Providers, processing locations and retention periods for the managed Brev Cloud service.">
<h2>1. Subprocessors</h2>
  <p>This list distinguishes infrastructure providers from services that are internal, do not process service users' data or are not enabled.</p>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Entity</th><th>Role</th><th>Data processed</th><th>Location and safeguards</th><th>Reference</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Cloudflare, Inc.</td><td>CDN, DNS, TLS termination, WAF and Cloudflare for SaaS for customer domains.</td><td>Visitors' IP addresses and traffic for the website and customer domains.</td><td>United States. The customer DPA includes the European Commission's standard contractual clauses for transfers.</td><td><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-customer-dpa/">Customer DPA</a></td></tr>
        <tr><td>IONOS SE</td><td>Hosting of application servers and the database on VPS infrastructure.</td><td>Account, link, domain and click data stored by the service.</td><td>Germany. Processing in the European Union.</td><td>Application and database hosting.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Contabo GmbH</td><td>Hosting of the transactional mail server <code>mail.novezero.it</code>.</td><td>Recipient email addresses and service emails for verification, password resets, email changes and domain invitations.</td><td>Germany. Processing in the European Union.</td><td><a href="https://contabo.com/en/legal/privacy/">Privacy notice</a></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Plausible self-hosted</td><td>Cookieless statistics for the landing and legal pages only.</td><td>No personal data retained. IP addresses are used only to derive country and are not retained. No profiling.</td><td>Controller's infrastructure at novezero.it, under the same controller. No analytics data transferred to third parties. Not a subprocessor.</td><td>Self-hosted, not a third-party provider.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>GitHub, Inc.</td><td>Public repository and security reports.</td><td>Does not process service users' data.</td><td>Not a processor of Brev Cloud user data.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/brevlink/brev">Public repository</a></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Stripe</td><td>Not enabled.</td><td>No payment data processed today.</td><td>Any activation will be documented beforehand.</td><td>No active payment service.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>For Brev self-hosted, each operator is the controller and must compile their own provider list for their installation.</p>

  <h2>2. Retention</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Period and deletion</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Account and profile</td><td>For the life of the account. Removed immediately through self-service account deletion.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Links, domains and domain memberships</td><td>For the life of the account. Link deletion removes the link and its related data; account deletion removes owned domains and memberships as well.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Raw click events</td><td>90 days, configurable by a self-hosted operator with <code>CLICK_EVENT_RETENTION_DAYS</code>. Removed with the link or account.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Daily click aggregates</td><td>No automatic expiry. Removed with the link or account.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Sessions</td><td>Until logout, expiry or revocation. Invalidated on account deletion.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Single-use tokens</td><td>Verification, password reset, email change and domain invitation tokens are stored as hashes, consumed on first use and have a technical expiry. Email change links last 24 hours; domain invitations last 14 days. Removed on account deletion.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Support messages</td><td>For the time needed to handle the request and keep a record of it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>CDN, hosting and mail logs</td><td>Under Cloudflare, IONOS and Contabo policies. Their retention periods are not set by Brev.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Infrastructure backups, if active</td><td>Copies may remain for the backup rotation cycle. Used only for recovery after a failure.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Billing data</td><td>None today. If payments are enabled, accounting documents will be retained for the period required by Italian law and this page will be updated.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>3. Changes to this list</h2>
  <p>The version and last updated date appear above. New providers will be published on this page with an updated version and date. Self-hosted operators maintain their own lists.</p>
</LegalLayout>
